eek this 50/50 equilibrium that's  not true it's every flip seeks this  50/50 equilibrium and as well as we'll  find with the scenario that we're going  to do now it is simply not the case that  just because you know something occurs  you know a bunch of times even with  50/50 odds it does not mean that the  next thing will be yeah the opposite so  again with our example in mind just  remember of the big user roles 1/2 a 50  the house wins 50 1 to 99 the user wins  and a perfect 100 means the house wins  so let's go ahead and begin so first we  have to generate our actual dies and for  this we're gonna first can employ the  pseudo-random number generator within  Python so let's go ahead and get started  so we're gonna import  that's odd there we go  import random and now we're going to  define roll dice no parameters for this  and we're just going to say role equals  random dot R and int so this is just a  random integer between 1 and 100 and  that's it so then at the end of this  we'll return the roll and that's it for  now so now let's go ahead and just  quickly test our dice to make sure it's  giving us what we want so we're just  gonna say x equals 0 while X is less  than 100 results equals roll dice print  results and then X plus equals 1 sounds  good  we'll save and run this and sure enough  here is our output  here so here's obviously a one and then  a bunch of numbers I don't see a 100 but  it was possible we just didn't get one  so now that we have a dice done what we  want now is we need a better so we need  to make just a simple better in our  program so that's what we're going to be  doing in the next video is creating our  better  who's going to bet on this dice roll so  anyway stay tuned to the next video as  always thanks for watching thanks for  all the support and subscriptions until  next time
 

